## Probes that found nothing (with the stdout that shows it)

**`load_model` mis-merge.** Script `/tmp/ledger_fold_review/probes/probe_load_model.py`, stdout `/tmp/ledger_fold_review/probes/probe_load_model_stdout.txt`. Chronological last-wins, F9b audit, two-delta collision, and no F9 re-prefix all matched the contract. Out-of-order deltas last-win in the *given* order (caller chronology, not a fold bug).

```
PROBE chronological_last_wins OBSERVED {'shared_value': 5, 'shared_step': 'D2', ..., 'overwrites': [('shared', 'BASE', 'D1'), ('shared', 'D1', 'D2'), ('d1_only', 'D1', 'D2')], ...}
PROBE f9b_overwrite_audit OBSERVED {..., 'audit_equals_expected': True}
PROBE no_f9_reapply OBSERVED {'x_present': True, 's11c_c1_x_present': True, 'x_value': 10, 's11c_c1_x_value': 11, 'extra_keys': [], 'x_not_overwritten': True}
PROBE key_in_two_deltas_not_in_base OBSERVED {'fresh_value': 2, 'fresh_step': 'DB', 'overwrites': [('fresh', 'DA', 'DB')]}
```

**Two-deep dimension/symbol closure in the implementation** — caught (must-fix 1 is the *tests*, not the walker). Nested Matrix/Tuple/relational Symbol atoms — caught.

---

**Verdict:** must-fix holes — recursive-closure tests are tautological, and an F9c symbol edge to an expression-valued predecessor is a silent mis-route the guard and its F9c test both miss.
